   "body": "## AWJ-HORIZON-V2-1B — Authority & Threat Model\n\n**Documentation only.** No merge, deploy, Ruleset, Branch Protection, Auto-Merge, GitHub permission change, or grant is enabled. V2-2/3/4 not started. No other Horizon touched.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Base SHA | `b3dc3d8e68a127dfd2ca5d1c3f50e4e5a8676ffd` |\n| Head SHA | `473f6a83a1c0b2f9edbcd1efcaf564906c6734cb` (supersedes `cb6c381`; results for the earlier SHA are not relied on) |\n\n### Contents\n- `AWJ-HORIZON-V2-1B-AUTHORITY-THREAT-MODEL.md` — Zones A/B/C/P, Grant Schema + fail-closed evaluation, Threat Model T1–T10, GitHub safety plan G0–G5 (explicitly **not enabled**), parallel-horizon registry, dry-run contract (**11 scenarios / 23 test cases**), Decision Packet D1–D10.\n- `AWJ-HORIZON-V2-1B-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT.md` — final report.\n- `AWJ-HORIZON-AUTONOMY-V2-PROPOSAL.md` — one-line pointer in §10.\n\n### Corrections in this head\n- Dry-run counts unified and verified against the table (previously \"25 sub-cases\"/\"ten cases\" inconsistently).\n- §4.6: a signed commit alone does **not** prove grant authenticity (GitHub signs merge commits; a signature proves key possession, not owner intent). Owner identity verification out-of-band, isolated keys, pinned `allowed_signers`, content binding, and rotation/revocation are mandatory.\n- §7: table stating every protection (Ruleset, Required Check, Require PR, gate-file protection, independent review, Auto-Merge) is currently **not enabled**.\n\n### Checks\n`ci-gate` self-tests 49/49 OK · `git diff --check` clean · `php artisan test` runs in CI on this head. No financial operations → no accounting entries.\n\nMerge authority is the owner's alone.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01X2ShKtNyjEJkNK5m7yC6BU",
